[2026-06-02 23:54:30] [INFO] [PostToolBatch] Input: {"session_id":"1b51e036-fd80-4ff2-ab54-87dea13ff9e7","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\1b51e036-fd80-4ff2-ab54-87dea13ff9e7.jsonl","cwd":"D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk","permission_mode":"plan","effort":{"level":"medium"},"hook_event_name":"PostToolBatch","tool_calls":[{"tool_name":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"Read all 5 doc files","prompt":"Read the following 5 documentation files completely and summarize each one's content, structure, and key sections:\n\n1. D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\doc\\otherDoc\\2026-06-01\\2026-06-01-可视化页面线框图设计-v2.md\n2. D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\doc\\otherDoc\\2026-06-01\\2026-06-01-backend功能设计.md\n3. D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\doc\\otherDoc\\2026-06-01\\2026-06-01-BDD测试用例.md\n4. D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\doc\\otherDoc\\2026-06-01\\2026-06-01-hook状态展示机制.md\n5. D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\doc\\otherDoc\\2026-06-01\\2026-06-01-hooks设计文档.md\n\nFor each file, list:\n- The main sections and their content\n- Any references to backend APIs, endpoints, or data structures\n- Any references to hooks, status tracking, or proxy functionality\n- Areas that seem incomplete or marked as TODO\n","subagent_type":"Explore"},"tool_use_id":"call_91f7d75e92354fe1b8aad65c","tool_response":[{"type":"text","text":"\n## Summary of Documentation Files\n\n### 1. **2026-06-01-可视化页面线框图设计-v2.md**\n\n**Main Sections**:\n- **API Inventory** (Section II): Lists 10 existing API endpoints with their request/response formats\n- **Data Models** (Section III): Go structs for IssueClaim, Session, Machine, and Project tables\n- **Page Design** (Section III): UI wireframes for 5 pages using ASCII art\n- **Global Components** (Section IV): Navigation bar and status color scheme\n- **Data Flow Design** (Section V): Sequence diagrams for session and issue management flows\n- **API Gaps** (Section VI): 12 missing APIs needed for full functionality\n\n**Key Backend References**:\n- **Issue APIs**: `/api/issue/check`, `/api/issue/claim`, `/api/issue/release`, `/api/issue/status`\n- **Session APIs**: `/api/session/register`, `/api/session/close`, `/api/sessions`, `/api/session/{id}`\n- **Proxy APIs**: `/api/proxy/register`, `/api/proxy/unregister`, `/api/proxy/trace-init`\n- **Health Check**: `/health`\n\n**Hook/Status References**:\n- No direct hook references, but mentions status tracking through existing APIs\n- Status color scheme for issue states (idle: yellow, claimed: blue, fixing: orange, etc.)\n\n**Incomplete Areas**:\n- Multiple \"No API available\" labels for statistics (machine count, project count, issue totals)\n- TODO items for backend API extensions in Section VI\n\n---\n\n### 2. **2026-06-01-backend功能设计.md**\n\n**Main Sections**:\n- **System Overview** (Section I): Go + SQLite HTTP API service description\n- **Existing Modules** (Section II): Issue management, Session management, Proxy management\n- **Data Models** (Section III): Detailed database schema for 4 tables\n- **Extensible Features** (Section IV): Proposed new modules for machines, projects, issue queries, traces, monitoring\n- **API Design Specifications** (Section V): Response formats, pagination, filtering\n- **Technology Stack** (Section VI): Go 1.23+, SQLite, net/http\n- **Deployment** (Section VII): CLI subprocess auto-start with idle watchdog\n\n**Key Backend APIs**:\n- **Issue Management**: Check, Claim, Release, Release-session, Status update with optimistic locking\n- **Session Lifecycle**: Register, Close, List, Get details with active/closed states\n- **Proxy Management**: Register, Unregister, Trace-init forwarding\n- **Infrastructure**: IdleWatchdog, CleanupService\n\n**Hook Integration**:\n- Session registration on startup\n- Issue release on session end\n- Trace initialization through proxy forwarding\n\n**Incomplete Areas**:\n- Monitoring module (no system status API)\n- Configuration management (no GET/PUT config endpoints)\n- Trace file management (no listing/token statistics APIs)\n\n---\n\n### 3. **2026-06-01-BDD测试用例.md**\n\n**Main Sections**:\n- **Backend API BDD** (Section I): 13 features with 45 scenarios (positive/negative tests)\n- **Hooks System BDD** (Section II): 5 features with 14 scenarios for lifecycle events\n- **Visual Page BDD** (Section III): 5 features with 22 scenarios for UI interactions\n- **Implementation Status** (Section IV):对照表 showing which APIs are implemented\n- **Test Statistics** (Section V): 23 features, 81 scenarios total\n\n**Key Backend APIs Tested**:\n- All existing APIs from backend design doc are covered\n- Includes edge cases like concurrent claims, session cleanup, proxy failures\n\n**Hook Testing**:\n- **Session-start Hook**: Environment setup, backend registration\n- **Session-end Hook**: Issue release, session unregistration\n- **User-prompt-submit Hook**: Skill injection with registry matching\n- **Pre-tool-use Hook**: Permission control, boundary enforcement\n- **Stop Hook**: Skill registration, cleanup scripts\n\n**API Implementation Status**:\n- ✅ All 13 backend APIs implemented\n- ❌ 12 missing APIs for full functionality (issues, machines, projects, traces, logs, etc.)\n\n---\n\n### 4. **2026-06-01-hook状态展示机制.md**\n\n**Main Sections**:\n- **4 Display Mechanisms**: systemMessage, statusLine, statusMessage, terminalSequence\n- **Usage Scenarios**: When to use each mechanism\n- **Code Examples**: Bash implementations for each mechanism\n- **Combination Strategy**: Recommended usage patterns\n\n**Hook Integration**:\n- **systemMessage**: Direct feedback in chat flow\n- **statusLine**: Persistent status bar with state files\n- **statusMessage**: Loading indicators during hook execution\n- **terminalSequence**: Desktop notifications via escape sequences\n\n**State Management**:\n- State files in `.claude/hooks/state/`\n- Functions for writing hook states (`write_hook_state`, `write_backend_state`)\n- Color-coded status display (green/yellow/red)\n\n**Windows-Specific**:\n- PowerShell for window foregrounding\n- OSC 9 protocol for notifications\n- Task completion notifications\n\n---\n\n### 5. **2026-06-01-hooks设计文档.md**\n\n**Main Sections**:\n- **System Overview** (Section I): Hook system goals and architecture\n- **Architecture Design** (Section II): Directory structure and execution flow\n- **Core Modules** (Section III): Base framework, platform detection, backend integration\n- **Hook Events** (Section IV): 29 events categorized by frequency\n- **Skill Integration** (Section V): Activation mechanism and lifecycle scripts\n- **Windows Features** (Section VI): Window foregrounding system\n- **Backend Interaction** (Section VII): Session lifecycle and issue workflows\n\n**Key Hook Events**:\n- **Session Lifecycle**: 01-session-start, 29-session-end\n- **Round Level**: 03-user-prompt-submit (Skill injection), 16-stop (Skill registration)\n- **Tool Level**: 05-pre-tool-use (permission control), 06-permission-request\n- **Environment**: 02-setup, 20-config-change, etc.\n\n**Skill System**:\n- Registry-based skill matching\n- Activation state management (`.active` file)\n- Lifecycle script mapping (02-29 numbered scripts)\n- Concurrent control with file locks\n\n**Backend Integration**:\n- Session registration on startup\n- Issue management through skills\n- Trace initialization via proxy forwarding\n\n---\n\n## Common Themes and Gaps\n\n**Backend Dependencies**:\n- All documents rely on a Go backend with SQLite\n- Core APIs for issue management and session tracking are implemented\n- Missing APIs for statistics (machines, projects, issues), trace management, and system monitoring\n\n**Hook Architecture**:\n- Comprehensive hook system with 29 events\n- Skill injection mechanism for extensibility\n- Windows-specific features (window management, notifications)\n- Status tracking through multiple display mechanisms\n\n**Visual Design**:\n- Dashboard with real-time session metrics\n- Issue management interface with state tracking\n- Machine/project information extraction from session data\n- System status monitoring panel\n\n**Major TODO Items**:\n1. Implement missing backend APIs for full functionality\n2. Complete status line integration with state files\n3. Add desktop notification system\n4. Enhance error handling and fallback mechanisms\n5. Implement performance optimizations for hook execution"}]},{"tool_name":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"Read recent backend code changes","prompt":"Explore the recent backend code changes in the claude_tap_plus/ directory. Read these files thoroughly:\n\n1. claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/api/proxy_handler.go\n2. claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/api/response.go\n3. claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/api/status_handler.go\n4. claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/api/router.go\n5. claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/service/proxy_service.go\n6. claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/service/status_service.go\n7. claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/store/proxy_store.go\n8. claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/store/migrations.go\n9. claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/store/store.go\n10. claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/store/sqlite.go\n11. claude_tap_plus/internal/backend/server.go\n12. claude_tap_plus/tests/backend/proxy_list_api_test.go\n13. claude_tap_plus/tests/backend/status_api_test.go\n\nFor each file, summarize:\n- What new APIs/endpoints were added\n- What new data structures (request/response types) were defined\n- What new database tables or migrations were added\n- What new service logic was implemented\n- The full API route map (method + path + handler)\n","subagent_type":"Explore"},"tool_use_id":"call_a93b4b92aa474f20b453715c","tool_response":[{"type":"text","text":"\nBased on my thorough analysis of the recent backend code changes in the claude_tap_plus/ directory, here's a comprehensive summary:\n\n## Summary of Recent Backend Changes\n\n### 1. **New APIs/Endpoints Added**\n\n#### Proxy Management APIs:\n- **POST /api/proxy/register** - Register a proxy\n  - Request body: `{\"pid\": \"28364\", \"proxy_url\": \"http://127.0.0.1:64902\"}`\n  - Response: `{\"status\": \"ok\"}`\n  \n- **POST /api/proxy/unregister** - Unregister a proxy\n  - Request body: `{\"pid\": \"28364\"}`\n  - Response: `{\"status\": \"ok\"}`\n  \n- **POST /api/proxy/trace-init** - Forward trace-init requests to all registered proxies\n  - Forwards request body to each proxy's `/_internal/trace-init`\n  - Returns first successful response\n  \n- **GET /api/proxies** - List all registered proxies\n  - Query params: `?status=<active|offline>`, `?project=<slug>`\n  - Response: `{\"proxies\": [...], \"total\": N}`\n\n#### System Status API:\n- **GET /api/status** - Get overall system status\n  - Returns health status, version, uptime, and statistics\n  - Response includes active sessions, proxies, pending issues, machines, and projects\n\n### 2. **New Data Structures**\n\n#### Proxy-Related Types:\n- `ProxyItem` - Single proxy entry in list response\n  ```go\n  type ProxyItem struct {\n      ProxyID      string     `json:\"proxy_id\"`\n      ProjectSlug  string     `json:\"project_slug\"`\n      Status       string     `json:\"status\"`\n      RegisteredAt time.Time  `json:\"registered_at\"`\n      LastPingAt   *time.Time `json:\"last_ping_at,omitempty\"`\n  }\n  ```\n\n- `ProxiesResponse` - Wrapper for proxy list response\n  ```go\n  type ProxiesResponse struct {\n      Proxies []ProxyItem `json:\"proxies\"`\n      Total   int         `json:\"total\"`\n  }\n  ```\n\n#### System Status Types:\n- `StatusResponse` - System status response structure\n  ```go\n  type StatusResponse struct {\n      Status        string       `json:\"status\"`\n      Version       string       `json:\"version\"`\n      UptimeSeconds int64        `json:\"uptime_seconds\"`\n      Stats         SystemStats  `json:\"stats\"`\n      Timestamp     time.Time    `json:\"timestamp\"`\n  }\n  ```\n\n- `SystemStats` - System statistics aggregation\n  ```go\n  type SystemStats struct {\n      ActiveSessions int64 `json:\"active_sessions\"`\n      ActiveProxies  int64 `json:\"active_proxies\"`\n      PendingIssues  int64 `json:\"pending_issues\"`\n      TotalMachines  int64 `json:\"total_machines\"`\n      TotalProjects  int64 `json:\"total_projects\"`\n  }\n  ```\n\n### 3. **New Database Tables/Migrations**\n\n#### `proxies` Table:\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE proxies (\n    proxy_id      TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n    project_slug  TEXT NOT NULL,\n    status        TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active',\n    registered_at DATETIME NOT NULL,\n    last_ping_at  DATETIME\n);\n```\n\n- Indexes created on `status` and `project_slug` columns\n- Supports filtering by status and project in queries\n\n### 4. **New Service Logic**\n\n#### ProxyService:\n- `List(ctx, filter)` - Retrieve proxies with optional status/project filtering\n- Maintains in-memory registry for quick access\n- Handles concurrent access with mutex protection\n\n#### StatusService:\n- `Get(ctx)` - Aggregates system-wide statistics\n- Counts active sessions, proxies, pending issues, machines, and projects\n- Calculates uptime since server start\n\n### 5. **Full API Route Map**\n\n```\nHealth Check:\nGET /health\n\nIssue Management:\nGET  /api/issue/check           - Check issue status\nPOST /api/issue/claim          - Claim issue\nPOST /api/issue/release        - Release issue\nPOST /api/issue/release-session - Release all issues for session\nPOST /api/issue/status         - Update issue status\nGET  /api/issues              - List all issues\n\nSession Management:\nPOST /api/session/register     - Register session\nPOST /api/session/close       - Close session\nGET  /api/sessions             - List sessions\nGET  /api/session/{id}/issues  - Get session issues\nGET  /api/session/{id}/tokens   - Get session token stats\nGET  /api/session/{id}/traces   - Get session trace files\nGET  /api/session/{id}          - Get session details\n\nProxy Management (NEW):\nPOST /api/proxy/register      - Register proxy\nPOST /api/proxy/unregister    - Unregister proxy\nPOST /api/proxy/trace-init    - Forward trace-init\nGET  /api/proxies             - List proxies (with optional filters)\n\nMachine Management:\nGET  /api/machines            - List machines\n\nProject Management:\nGET  /api/projects            - List projects\n\nLog Management:\nGET  /api/logs                - Query logs\n\nConfiguration:\nGET/PUT /api/config          - Get/update config\n\nSystem Status (NEW):\nGET  /api/status              - Get system status\n```\n\n### 6. **Key Features Implemented**\n\n1. **Proxy Management**: Full CRUD operations for proxy registration and management\n2. **Distributed Trace Init**: Centralized forwarding of trace-init requests to multiple proxies\n3. **System Monitoring**: Comprehensive status endpoint with aggregated statistics\n4. **Query Filtering**: Support for filtering proxies by status and project\n5. **Memory + Database**: Dual storage with in-memory cache for performance and persistent storage\n6. **Concurrency Safety**: Mutex protection for proxy operations\n\nThe implementation follows clean architecture principles with clear separation between API handlers, business logic services, and data storage layers. All new endpoints include proper error handling, validation, and BDD-style test coverage."}]}]}
